--- !u!114 &7836131044221255207
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>The fog-only lights.</b> The Fog Spots carry most of the haze under the canopy, but they should not light the surfaces a second time. The fog feature ignores <b>Rendering Layers</b>, while surfaces respect them. So the Fog Spots are set to a Rendering Layer that no object uses (<i>Light \u203A Rendering \u203A Rendering Layers</i>, a spare layer, for example layer 15), and their shadows keep the default layers, so the canopy, the columns and the pumps still cut their light into shafts. Their short Range (8 m) ends the bright haze about where the canopy ends."
